# Models fetched by scripts/fetch_models.sh (zoo compile pinned by sha256).
# Vendored files in this directory (no rows here) are exact device artifacts
# committed via the .gitignore negation:
#   - hailo_yolov8n_384_640.hef — 5-class security compile (sidecar
#     hailo_yolov8n_384_640.json: unlabeled/person/vehicle/face/
#     license_plate, label_offset 1) as shipped on the devices; the zoo
#     compile of the same name is NOT the same artifact, so it is vendored
#     - exact bytes probed on 93.72 2026-09-22 (parking-lot scenes: 8-21
#     vehicle boxes @0.3-0.79 conf, ~38ms/frame)
#   - yolov5m_vehicles.hef — legacy 1-class 1080p compile (variant-coupled
#     NMS; the generic zoo yolov5m would mismatch the postprocess config);
#     vehicle detector through 1.2.1, kept vendored for device-side A/B
#   - tiny_yolov4_license_plates.hef — license-plate detector, no zoo build
#   - paddle_ocr_v5_mobile_recognition_nv12.hef — plate OCR, no zoo build
#   - yolov8n_vehicle_det.bin / scdepthv3.bin / license_plate_det.bin /
#     plate_recognition.bin — AMPK packages (app.yaml spec.models paths)
#     exported from the platform model rows via platform-api
#     `GET /api/v1/ai/models/:model_id/export`; the embedded HEF bytes are
#     identical to the vendored .hef above, so the packages stay in sync
#     with the artifacts the app registers at runtime. Regenerate after
#     replacing any .hef (the package metadata pins the HEF sha256).
#     yolov8n_vehicle_det.bin pins the hailo_yolov8n_384_640
#     postprocess_profile whose default hailo_yolov8n backend matches the
#     HEF's NMS tensor, so preloads already route correctly.
#     license_plate_det.bin exports output_mode raw — the app decodes the
#     yolov4 grid itself, and the default detection profile pinned in its
#     package config is inert on that path. yolov5m_vehicles.bin was
#     dropped in 1.2.2 together with its spec.models/permissions entries
#     (preload walks permissions and would 6002 on fresh devices).
# Zoo pinning rationale: v5.3.0/hailo15h matches the device firmware
# (HailoRT 5.3.0). Re-verify with `hailortcli parse-hef` before bumping.
0c7c7e5958e75f722bd3355106dba21d2c13f737dab3f627701844b34ed9f7e7	scdepthv3.hef	https://hailo-model-zoo.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/ModelZoo/Compiled/v5.3.0/hailo15h/scdepthv3.hef
